      "writtenOn": "2018-09-13T20:46:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree that these are both NaN, there are many forms of quiet NaN.  I just think that the compatibility with hardware floating-point will be better if you use the hardware\u0027s default quiet NaN instead of a different (yet still valid) NaN.",
      "parentUuid": "c440faab_d9f13932",
